How do we derive the resource limits of an pod application?
-----------------------------------------------------------------
Neither the devops engineer nor the developer can define or decide the resources (cpu & memory) that needs to be alloted to the pod application. Usually the application would be put for performance testing with performance engineering team, for deriving the bench mark metrix of cpu and memory usage levels of the application. The team generates virtual traffic simulating the real-world traffic to the application and derives the min & max resource requirements

apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  name: hangoutpod
spec:
  containers:
    - name: hangout
      image: hangout:1.0
      ports:
        - name: hangoutport
          containerPort: 8080
          protocol: TCP
      readinessProbe:
        httpGet:
          path: /hangout/actuator/health/readiness
          port: 8080
        initialDelaySeconds: 3
        timeoutSeconds: 10
        failureThreshold: 3
      livenessProbe:
        httpGet:
          path: /hangout/actuator/health/liveness
          port: 8080
        initialDelaySeconds: 5
        timeoutSeconds: 10
        failureThreshold: 3
      resources:
        requests:
          cpu: "500m"
          memory: "512Mi"
        limits:
          cpu: "1000m"
          memory: "1024Mi"

